 "answer": "To find $71^{390} \\pmod{233}$:\n\n1. Compute small powers of $71 \\pmod{233}$:\n   - $71^2 = 5041 = 21 \\times 233 + 148 \\equiv 148 \\equiv -85 \\pmod{233}$\n   - $71^4 \\equiv (-85)^2 = 7225 = 31 \\times 233 + 2 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{233}$\n\n2. Express $71^{390}$ in terms of $71^4$:\n   - $390 = 4 \\times 97 + 2$\n   - $71^{390} = (71^4)^{97} \\times 71^2 \\equiv 2^{97} \\times 148 \\pmod{233}$\n\n3. Determine the order of $2 \\pmod{233}$:\n   - $2^8 = 256 \\equiv 23 \\pmod{233}$\n   - $2^{16} \\equiv 23^2 = 529 \\equiv 63 \\pmod{233}$\n   - $2^{24} = 63 \\times 23 = 1449 \\equiv 51 \\pmod{233}$\n   - $2^{29} = 51 \\times 32 = 1632 = 7 \\times 233 + 1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{233}$\n\n4. Reduce $2^{97} \\pmod{233}$:\n   - $97 = 3 \\times 29 + 10 \\implies 2^{97} \\equiv 2^{10} = 1024 = 4 \\times 233 + 92 \\equiv 92 \\pmod{233}$\n\n5. Multiply the components:\n   - $71^{390} \\equiv 92 \\times 148 \\equiv 92 \\times (-85) = -7820 \\pmod{233}$\n   - $-7820 = -34 \\times 233 + 102 \\equiv 102 \\pmod{233}$\n\nFINAL: 102"
